{
  "info": {
    "name": "Bank App API - Test Collection (DRAFT)",
    "description": "DRAFT - grounded against the main-branch source but not yet executed end-to-end; the first run may need small fixes.\n\nExecutable API test collection for the Online Banking Mini Application (Go/Gin + PostgreSQL, base path /api). Run the WHOLE collection in folder order with the Collection Runner or Newman, against a DISPOSABLE backend instance on port 8081 backed by the bankdb_test database - see the setup steps that came with this file. Do NOT run it against your normal app database: it mutates data (creates a beneficiary, moves Rs 1.00 between demo accounts, marks a transfer UNDER_REVIEW, assigns an account to demo-operations, freezes and unfreezes an account; if a run aborts mid-pair the account stays frozen).\n\nMechanics: test scripts capture the CSRF token from each login response (meta.csrfToken) and the session id from Set-Cookie, and a collection-level pre-request script sends the session cookie explicitly (some HTTP clients do not store Secure cookies over plain http://localhost, so this does not rely on cookie-jar behavior).\n\nCovered: auth per role, accounts, a BOLA 404 check, beneficiary lifecycle, transfers with idempotency replay, operations review + freeze/unfreeze, admin reads, CSRF-missing 403, and session-expired 401. Deliberately excluded (state-changing and covered by the automated Go API test suite): admin user creation, role/status changes, password resets, limit changes, and signup.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const sid = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"sessionId\");",
          "if (sid) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: \"Cookie\", value: \"session_id=\" + sid });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
